      "message": "I\u0027m concerned about how this interacts with soong namespaces -- this isn\u0027t respecting the soong namespace -- we\u0027ll get a global list of all possible vendor_public_library modules. If the name had been marked as a vendor_public_library in some unused namespace, that could break the build if it wasn\u0027t marked as public in the current namespaces.\n\nFor Make, we need to filter that list to only vendor_public_library modules that are exported to Make. A bit more work, but shouldn\u0027t be too bad.\n\nFor Soong (cc.go), we\u0027d need to take into account the visible namespaces from the current module somehow. Maybe we\u0027ll need to probe w/OtherModuleExists?",
